{"name":"St. Nicholas Beard","hex":"#eedddd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"st.","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of St., abbreviation of street."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/st."},{"term":"beard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Facial hair on the chin, cheeks, jaw and neck.","The cluster of small feathers at the base of the beak in some birds."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow hair on the chin and jaw.","To boldly and bravely oppose or confront, often to the chagrin of the one being bearded."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nick Beard","blocks":[{"text":"Nicholas Brendan Beard is a New Zealand former professional cricketer. He played as a left-handed batsman and left-arm slow bowler for Otago. He was born at Dunedin and educated at Kavanagh College."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nick_Beard"},{"title":"Saint Nicholas","blocks":[{"text":"Saint Nicholas of Myra, also known as Nicholas of Bari, was an early Christian bishop of Greek descent from the maritime city of Patara in Anatolia during the time of the Roman Empire. Because of the many miracles attributed to his intercession, he is also known as Nicholas the Wonderworker. Saint Nicholas is the patron saint of sailors, merchants, archers, repentant thieves, children, brewers, pawnbrokers, toymakers, unmarried people, and students in various cities and countries around Europe. His reputation evolved among the pious, as was common for early Christian saints, and his legendary habit of secret gift-giving gave rise to the folklore of Santa Claus through Sinterklaas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Jaroslav_%C4%8Cerm%C3%A1k_%281831_-_1878%29_-_Sv._Mikul%C3%A1%C5%A1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Jaroslav_%C4%8Cerm%C3%A1k_%281831_-_1878%29_-_Sv._Mikul%C3%A1%C5%A1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Nicholas"},{"title":"Nicholas","blocks":[{"text":"Nicholas is a male name, the Anglophone version of an ancient Greek name in use since antiquity, and cognate with the modern Greek Νικόλαος, Nikolaos. It originally derived from a combination of two Greek words meaning 'victory' and 'people'. In turn, the name means \"victory of the people.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Gheorghe_Tattarescu_-_Sfantul_Nicolae.jpg/330px-Gheorghe_Tattarescu_-_Sfantul_Nicolae.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicholas"},{"title":"Beard","blocks":[{"text":"A beard is the hair that grows on the jaw, chin, upper lip, lower lip, cheeks, and neck of humans and some non-human animals. In humans, beards are most common among pubescent and adult males, though some women also develop them in a condition called hirsutism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Photography-wallpaper-facial-hair-man-beard-chin-moustache-human-elder-portrait-1453095.jpg/330px-Photography-wallpaper-facial-hair-man-beard-chin-moustache-human-elder-portrait-1453095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beard"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Gentile_da_Fabriano_063.jpg/500px-Gentile_da_Fabriano_063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Gentile_da_Fabriano_063.jpg/1280px-Gentile_da_Fabriano_063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Gentile_da_Fabriano_063.jpg/500px-Gentile_da_Fabriano_063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The dowry for the three virgins (Gentile da Fabriano, c. 1425, Pinacoteca Vaticana, Rome)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGentile_da_Fabriano_063.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/S._Nicholas_by_T.Poulakis_%28%3F%29%2C_17th_c.jpg/500px-S._Nicholas_by_T.Poulakis_%28%3F%29%2C_17th_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/S._Nicholas_by_T.Poulakis_%28%3F%29%2C_17th_c.jpg/1280px-S._Nicholas_by_T.Poulakis_%28%3F%29%2C_17th_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/S._Nicholas_by_T.Poulakis_%28%3F%29%2C_17th_c.jpg/500px-S._Nicholas_by_T.Poulakis_%28%3F%29%2C_17th_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Icon of Saint Nicholas with scenes written by Theodore Poulakis (1650–1692)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AS._Nicholas_by_T.Poulakis_(%3F)%2C_17th_c.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Ilja_Jefimowitsch_Repin_-_Saint_Nicholas_of_Myra_saves_three_innocents_from_death.jpg/500px-Ilja_Jefimowitsch_Repin_-_Saint_Nicholas_of_Myra_saves_three_innocents_from_death.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Ilja_Jefimowitsch_Repin_-_Saint_Nicholas_of_Myra_saves_three_innocents_from_death.jpg/1280px-Ilja_Jefimowitsch_Repin_-_Saint_Nicholas_of_Myra_saves_three_innocents_from_death.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Ilja_Jefimowitsch_Repin_-_Saint_Nicholas_of_Myra_saves_three_innocents_from_death.jpg/500px-Ilja_Jefimowitsch_Repin_-_Saint_Nicholas_of_Myra_saves_three_innocents_from_death.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Saint N